Cell[TextData[{
 "The symbol page of each region carries its counts on the other lattices and \
its continuum expansion. A profile, the list of a measure over the size, is \
read by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["LogDifferenceQuotients"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/LogDifferenceQuotients", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "84dfad1a-b6ca-47b6-919c-2e5c99b6563c"],
 ". The quotients of the counting profile from ",
 StyleBox["r = 0", "TI"],
 " and of the Riemannian profile from ",
 StyleBox["r = 1", "TI"],
 " coincide on a lattice, and they are the curves of the technical \
introduction, section 4.5: on ",
 StyleBox["Z^d", "TI"],
 " they approach the dimension as ",
 StyleBox["d + d/(2r)", "TI"],
 ", from above, while the counting profile from ",
 StyleBox["r = 1", "TI"],
 " approaches it as ",
 StyleBox["d \[Minus] d/(2r)", "TI"],
 ", from below."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"423053ea-ad14-4938-b0ad-5ad12b7924bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Euclidean head is inert: it holds its points and options and computes \
nothing on its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b442978-f04f-4c16-9e86-6562232f1ea6"],
 " is what evaluates it, reading every property off the head's ",
 StyleBox["graph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] an acyclic directed graph whose source-to-sink chains are \
exactly the head's members \[LongDash] by one forward and one backward sweep \
of a dynamic-programming count, never by enumeration. A circle's graph is a \
",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7968a7d1-14af-45d8-b7a2-91ba30fba09b"],
 " of atoms of the unrolled band along a radial seam (necklaces where the cut \
band is disconnected or the seam has one side only; see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2bf3ea4c-07d2-4404-8b3c-62528cb06ac2"],
 "). Each is an acyclic DAG from a seam vertex ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " to a copy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "067c74b8-20db-4a2a-bdc7-028d5ab01d03"],
 " of it, so a circle is a chain read as a closed walk, ",
 StyleBox["opened",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " at ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ". A circle's member is the chain with the copy dropped, a cyclic vertex \
list whose first vertex is not repeated. The closed arc has the same shape on \
the atom at its point."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3050b5ea-4484-4dc2-bfbb-0e10f5be1058"],

Cell["The properties:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"24f93e4f-0a84-4d73-957c-4dcabcba6542"],

